Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when the pinned GNOME Build Meta junction declares firewalld's iptables dependency and command paths.
Subject: firewalld: provide iptables at build and runtime

Without iptables in the build sandbox, configure substitutes /bin/false for
its IPv4 and IPv6 commands, breaking direct rules used by Docker even with
the default nftables backend. Keep that backend and existing firewall policy.
Select the nft-compatible iptables executables explicitly rather than relying
on the generic aliases, which can select legacy binaries in older artifacts.

diff --git a/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst b/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst
--- a/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst
+++ b/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst
@@ -17,8 +17,16 @@ build-depends:
 - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/libxslt.bst
 
 depends:
+- freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/iptables.bst
 - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/python3-nftables.bst
 - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/python3.bst
 
+variables:
+  conf-local: >-
+    --with-iptables=/usr/bin/iptables-nft
+    --with-iptables-restore=/usr/bin/iptables-nft-restore
+    --with-ip6tables=/usr/bin/ip6tables-nft
+    --with-ip6tables-restore=/usr/bin/ip6tables-nft-restore
+
 environment:
   ACLOCAL_PATH: /usr/share/gettext/m4
